{"step_index":1171,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:36:53Z","thinking":"**Examining Conjecturing Pipeline Status**\n\nTheorem prover is part of the conjecturing pipeline. The current status shows 22 kernel-checked lemmas in the challenge file. Reviewing the report confirms a universally true conjecture with empirical verification up to graph size $n=7$ and tree size $n=1$.\n\n\n**Verifying Report Generation Requirements**\n\nThe report generation is essential for the verification process. The current focus must align with the specified report requirements and acceptance criteria for successful completion of the conjecture. Ensure that the required output files are correctly produced and the generated report includes the necessary summaries and the `check.sh` output.\n\n\n**Exploring Proof Completion Strategies**\n\nConsidering the goal `GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G`, the approach will use contradiction, starting with `by_contra hc`. The negation `hc` transforms the goal to `GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G ≤ GraphCalc.radius G`.  Deductions show `2 ≤ GraphCalc.radius G`.\n\nFurther analysis is needed to relate `romanDominationNumber G` to the radius. The existence of a Roman dominating function, where the roman weight equals the Roman domination number will be investigated.\n\n\n**Analyzing Roman Domination Number Constraints**\n\nExamining the impossibility of `romanWeight f ≤ radius G`. Initially considering cases for the set of vertices labeled 2, denoted S. If S is empty, deduce a contradiction via `card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two`.\n\nNext, the case where S contains a single vertex is evaluated, leading to another contradiction using `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_unique_two`. Then, explored the case where the cardinality of S is greater or equal to 2, leading to $\\text{radius } G \\ge 4$ and $\\text{romanWeight } f \\ge 4$.\n\nConsidering the case of |S| = 2. Recognizing every vertex labeled 0 must be adjacent to an element in S. Every vertex outside of the function's labeled vertices (V1) is within distance 1 of S.\n\n\n**Constructing Proof by Contradiction**\n\nDetermining the length of path $P$ between $u_1$ and $u_2$, the intermediate vertices and their relationship to $V_1$ is key. This path length is at most $3 + |V_1|$. Calculating the distances between a midpoint $v^*$ on path $P$ and any vertex x in V gives a bound on eccentricity.\n\nThe eccentricity of $v^*$ is derived, bounding $\\text{radius}(G)$ by  $\\text{romanWeight}(f) - 1$.  Contradiction arises from $\\text{romanWeight}(f) \\le \\text{radius}(G)$, so the contradiction implies the initial assumption must be false.\n\nGeneralizing with |S| = m, the bound $2m + |V_1| - 1$ leads to radius(G) $\\le$ romanWeight(f) - 1, thereby deriving a contradiction and completing the proof strategy.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > /mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/test_full.lean\\nimport Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\nopen GraphCalc\\n\\n-- Copy of Challenge_e20263a9.lean up to lemma definitions\\nEOF\\ncat Challenge_e20263a9.lean | sed '/theorem prove_e20263a9/,$d' > test_full.lean\\ncat << 'EOF' >> test_full.lean\\n\\nlemma ballWithin_one_eq_univ_of_adj_all {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (u : V)\\n    (h : ∀ w : V, w = u ∨ G.Adj u w) :\\n    ballWithin G 1 u = Finset.univ := by\\n  ext w\\n  simp only [Finset.mem_univ, iff_true]\\n  cases h w with\\n  | inl heq => rw [heq]; exact mem_ballWithin_one_self G u\\n  | inr hadj => exact mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj G u w hadj\\n\\nlemma radius_le_one_of_adj_all {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G) (u : V)\\n    (h : ∀ w : V, w = u ∨ G.Adj u w) :\\n    GraphCalc.radius G ≤ 1 := by\\n  have h1 : ballWithin G 1 u = Finset.univ := ballWithin_one_eq_univ_of_adj_all G u h\\n  unfold GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass at hnt\\n  unfold GraphCalc.order at hnt\\n  have h_card_ge : 1 ≤ Fintype.card V := by omega\\n  have hecc : GraphCalc.eccentricity G u ≤ 1 := by\\n    unfold GraphCalc.eccentricity\\n    exact minUpTo_le 1 h_card_ge h1\\n  have hrad := radius_le_eccentricity G u\\n  omega\\n\\nlemma radius_le_one_of_romanWeight_le_two {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\\n    (hrad : GraphCalc.HasRadius G)\\n    (hnt : GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G)\\n    (f : V → Fin 3) (hf : GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f)\\n    (hw : GraphCalc.romanWeight f ≤ 2) :\\n    GraphCalc.radius G ≤ 1 := by\\n  by_cases h_no2 : ∀ v : V, (f v : ℕ) ≠ 2\\n  · have hcard := card_le_romanWeight_of_no_two G f hf h_no2\\n    have hradcard := radius_add_one_le_card G hrad hnt\\n    omega\\n  · push Not at h_no2\\n    rcases h_no2 with ⟨u, hu2⟩\\n   \n<truncated 2300 bytes>","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"20000","toolAction":"\"Testing test_full.lean\"","toolSummary":"\"Check test_full.lean\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
